    "content": "Goal\n* Please change \"that shows\" to \"that show\" (the verb refers to \"images\", right?).\n\n* Consider changing \"of the fully constructed die that shows the geometric orientations of some of the faces\" to \"that show some of the faces of the fully constructed die\".\n\nInput\n* Line 1: Consider simplifying as:\n{{6}} face labels used on the die, in no particular order\n\nOutput\n* Consider simplifying the first point:\nTwo die templates are <<equal>> if their folded dice can be rotated to match.\n\nConstraints\n* Please add constraints for [[W]] and [[H]].\n\nCases\n* You are probably aware that [[W]] is incorrect in more than half of the cases.\n\n* Some cases include face labels that are also used as edge characters in the 3D images (/, \\, |, +, -, v). These require special attention. Currently:\n  • /: Validators 7, 9, 17\n  • \\: Validator 8, Test 18\n  • |: Test 19, Validator 20\n  • +: Test 21\n  • -: Validator 14, Test 24\n  • v: Validator 3, Test 19, Validator 23\n  \"/\" doesn't appear in tests and \"+\" doesn't appear in validators. The cases should be adjusted to ensure proper coverage.\n\nThanks.",
